      "seed": 1063631846,
      "version": 1832,
      "versionNonce": 1071738225,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793860473005,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. INNER JOIN\n\nAn INNER JOIN returns only the records that have matching values\nin both tables according to the specified join condition. If a\ncustomer has not placed any orders, that customer will not appear\nin the result.",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. INNER JOIN\n\nAn INNER JOIN returns only the records that have matching values in both tables according to the specified join condition. If a customer has not placed any orders, that customer will not appear in the result.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EXDbib8JsbdD8WUO0bs_f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1417.7777777777774,
      "y": 1587.0837720586742,
      "width": 857.0000000000005,
      "height": 227.07930367504815,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3NV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 906801126,
      "version": 1890,
      "versionNonce": 1226086225,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793860473005,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RIGHT JOIN\n\nA RIGHT JOIN returns all the records from the right table\n(orders), regardless of whether they have a matching record in\nthe left table (customers). If an order has a matching customer,\nthe customer information is included in the result. If an order\ndoes not have a matching customer, the customer-related columns\ncontain NULL values.",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RIGHT JOIN\n\nA RIGHT JOIN returns all the records from the right table (orders), regardless of whether they have a matching record in the left table (customers). If an order has a matching customer, the customer information is included in the result. If an order does not have a matching customer, the customer-related columns contain NULL values.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1JEtOeqLVkxjlRbpqWdf5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1415.7777777777774,
      "y": 1846.9389894825554,
      "width": 857.0000000000005,
      "height": 255.46421663442916,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3Nl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1027551334,
      "version": 2104,
      "versionNonce": 2047313201,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793860473005,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FULL OUTER JOIN\n\nA FULL OUTER JOIN returns all records from both tables,\nregardless of whether they have matching records in the other\ntable. If a record has a match, the matching data from both\ntables is combined. If a record has no match, the columns\nbelonging to the other table contain NULL values. Now in my SQL\nwe do union of left join and right join to achieve Full join but\nwe get inbuilt in the Postgres",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FULL OUTER JOIN\n\nA FULL OUTER JOIN returns all records from both tables, regardless of whether they have matching records in the other table. If a record has a match, the matching data from both tables is combined. If a record has no match, the columns belonging to the other table contain NULL values. Now in my SQL we do union of left join and right join to achieve Full join but we get inbuilt in the Postgres",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GR0BNljuVcT0RBjQt58JM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1419.5277777777774,
      "y": 2158.917105392007,
      "width": 857.0000000000005,
      "height": 198.69439071566714,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3Nt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 306730872,
      "version": 1997,
      "versionNonce": 1310832401,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793860473005,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CROSS JOIN\n\nA CROSS JOIN returns the Cartesian product of two tables, meaning\nthat every row from the first table is combined with every row\nfrom the second table. If the first table contains 3 rows and the\nsecond table contains 4 rows, the result will contain 3 × 4 = 12\nrows.",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CROSS JOIN\n\nA CROSS JOIN returns the Cartesian product of two tables, meaning that every row from the first table is combined with every row from the second table. If the first table contains 3 rows and the second table contains 4 rows, the result will contain 3 × 4 = 12 rows.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "s2eQSMV8kogbfIKkuJyRq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4435.222222222223,
      "y": -314.19444444444423,
      "width": 1208.6666666666667,
      "height": 170.30947775628613,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1383456708,
      "version": 749,
      "versionNonce": 1244484817,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793860613162,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What are CTEs in SQL?\nCTE (Common Table Expression) is a temporary, named result set that you define using the\nWITH keyword and use inside a SQL query.\n\nThink of it as creating a temporary result with a name so you can write complex queries in\nsmaller, more readable steps.",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What are CTEs in SQL?\nCTE (Common Table Expression) is a temporary, named result set that you define using the WITH keyword and use inside a SQL query.\n\nThink of it as creating a temporary result with a name so you can write complex queries in smaller, more readable steps.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OlgYEe93s22_f8GLQEHHB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2891.8888888888887,
      "y": 1464.4722222222222,
      "width": 918.6666666666667,
      "height": 56.76982591876204,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1086332412,
      "version": 503,
      "versionNonce": 567791871,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793860582751,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Correlated Subqueries in SQL\nA correlated subquery is a subquery that depends on the outer query.",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. Correlated Subqueries in SQL\nA correlated subquery is a subquery that depends on the outer query.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
