    {
      "id": "XPfQze2stOohBgB56CyO9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1553.5055623022554,
      "y": 3088.934980338002,
      "width": 1118.7866383524206,
      "height": 369.00386847195324,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "an",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 966675162,
      "version": 3251,
      "versionNonce": 1559773638,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793809733057,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In SQL, we can create multiple database users and give them different permissions\ndepending on what they are allowed to do.\n\nWe don't want every user to access everything in our database. So, we can create\ndifferent database users and assign permissions to them. These permissions are\ncommonly called Privileges.\n\nWe can grant permissions at different levels, depending on the database system:\n- Database level\n- Schema level\n- Table level\n- View level\n- Procedure or function level",
      "fontSize": 22.707930367504815,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In SQL, we can create multiple database users and give them different permissions depending on what they are allowed to do.\n\nWe don't want every user to access everything in our database. So, we can create different database users and assign permissions to them. These permissions are commonly called Privileges.\n\nWe can grant permissions at different levels, depending on the database system:\n- Database level\n- Schema level\n- Table level\n- View level\n- Procedure or function level",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
